WEBVTT

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:39.010
It's amazing... You'd never
even think we were on a ship.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.060
This is the renowned official
casino ship of Port Verlington.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.470
Apart from the casino,
there are restaurants, a pool bar,

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.740
and a beauty spa as well as
anything else you can imagine.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.010
Are those people all gamblers?

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.970
No no... Most of them are just
moderately rich with free time,

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.180
and looking to have a night
of dreams and excitement.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:02.100
By the way, where is Dante?
He doesn't seem to be around...

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.350
This way.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:48.830
Two pairs.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.930
My apologies, but I believe
this hand is mine.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.130
Three of a kind.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.140
Dammit...

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.180
Well, no big deal... This
game's just getting underway.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.100
The fun's just beginning.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.440
Yes. I'm looking forward to it.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.760
The longer one gambles, the
more interesting it becomes...

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.110
The same as a kiss.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.680
If you can beat me,

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.310
I'll give you a long kiss, the likes of
which you've never experienced before.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.350
That's something to look forward to.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.760
I'd better be careful not to
lose the clothes off my back here!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.380
The man who just won is Gold-Arm
Joe, said to have a "Golden Arm."

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.890
The woman across the table is also famous.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:36.210
It's said that she has the luck of a
goddess. She's known as "Lucky Amanda."

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.640
The elderly man next to her is "Santa Claus,"

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:43.080
a poker ace that they say
can read people's thoughts.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:51.190
All these people are trying to act so refined,
but their eyes are burning with greed.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.300
Well, are we ready for another game?

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.750
Please... Save my husband, Paul.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.530
He likes to gamble?

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.490
Yes, he was a straight-and-narrow
man before we got married...

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.980
But it's like he became a different person
all of a sudden, and got addicted to gambling.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.390
Gambling is like a sickness.
But there's one big difference.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.320
There is no medicine you
can take to cure yourself of it.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.890
You might as well just give up on him.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.900
Please! If my husband goes
on like this, he could be killed!

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.010
Come on...

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.970
Hey, don't be so cold, Dante.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:32.270
Huh?

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.060
You should always be nice to women.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:39.520
Plus, it may not sound like it,
but this job could be up your alley.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.200
Next one, please.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:56.840
Pass.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.460
R-Raise. I'll raise you 500.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.100
--Fold.
--I'm dropping out too.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:07.530
I'll call.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.440
Call.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:16.890
Three of a kind.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.200
Nothing.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.130
Sorry kids, full house.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:27.830
If this keeps up, it looks like I'll go
home with a bag full of money again tonight!

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.720
I see, so that's why you're
"Santa Claus." It's a clever nickname.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.090
Thank you.

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:36.680
When this game's over, let
me treat you to breakfast.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:41.590
Sure. That is, as long as you're not
thrown out by then for being flat broke.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.710
We have quite a collection of
inflated egos here, don't we...

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:52.060
By the way, have any of you heard
of a gambler known as "King"?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.320
Yes, one hears about him quite a lot of late.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:59.020
Apparently he's supposed to be a gambler
from hell who takes the lives of his opponents.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.760
Hmph! Nothing but silly rumors!

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.350
They certainly are.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:06.930
However, it is true that a certain number
of gamblers have died after losing to him.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.610
Who is this King?

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:13.090
Some say he is an aged
man with a white beard.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:16.610
Others say King is a
beautiful, charming woman.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:19.720
But the truth is that no one knows for sure.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:28.710
Yet if such a person actually existed,
wouldn't you love to try a game with them?

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.590
King?

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:34.060
Yes. It's said he's a
gambler who brings death.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:38.790
There have been a number of well-known
gamblers who've recently gone missing.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.270
The only common thread is...

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:46.930
They all went out to play cards,
and then they never came back.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:50.280
Before long there were rumors
all over the city with people saying

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:54.300
that anyone who plays
this "King" will end up dead.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:58.100
So, this "King" could be a devil?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.760
If that's true, I guess I
gotta gamble with the devil.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.600
You'd probably be better off not doing that.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.980
I mean, you totally suck at gambling.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.300
Can you recall how much
money you owe me right now?

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.090
That's just because I'm nice
to the women when I play.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:15.540
Hey Dante, when are you gonna pay
out for our game you lost to me earlier?

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.140
I'm nice to the women and children.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:22.350
But how do I find a guy when I
don't even know what he looks like?

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:24.560
If I just randomly play cards looking for
him, it could take an infinite amount of time.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.730
--And infinite money.
--Shut up.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.140
A letter?

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:34.260
It's an invitation to that luxury cruise ship
turned casino operating in the next town over.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.910
It was sent by "King."

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:42.340
Since he went to the trouble to invite
us, it would be bad form not to accept.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.310
And since you'll be going anyhow,
you can grant that woman's request.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:48.470
You did say you're nice to
women and children, didn't you?

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:49.360
Damn.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:56.530
I don't know who this "King" guy is,
but he seems like a stuck-up snob.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.760
But it's interesting.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:04.350
If "King" is really here
among us, and I beat him,

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.470
my reputation will soar even higher.

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:11.700
Yeah, if King is among us,
you'll eventually find out.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:15.740
3,000.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.060
Fold. I'm out.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.640
I fold, too.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.140
I don't have enough chips.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.060
Well then, I guess you'll just
have to sit there and watch quietly.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:24.710
I'll raise...

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.470
I'll raise 5,000.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.680
Ohhh! The game is on!

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.040
Hey, you.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.470
You're shaking.

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:37.820
Don't you think you'd better go home,
before you make your pretty wife cry?

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:39.640
Leave me alone! Just be quiet!

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:40.770
Well, let's see 'em.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:44.390
He's holding three of a kind...

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:47.850
his face down card
could give him a full house...

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:49.770
Just to be safe...

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.620
All ready. I'm in for everything.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.950
Well, it's time for a showdown then.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.130
Full house!

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.830
F-Four of a kind!

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.650
I... I did it... I won! I won!

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:15.430
I won!

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:21.070
Th-That's not...

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:23.940
Sir?

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:28.870
He's dead...

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:33.110
Could this possibly mean that you are "King"?

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.110
N-No!

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:35.910
What are you saying?

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:37.700
I... I'm...

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:41.250
Just take it easy... Let's take a breather.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.350
Miss, call the person in charge.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.600
And I'd like a hot cappuccino, too.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.720
Right away, sir.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:51.680
Wherever King appears, that
place is governed by Death's rules.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.260
Maybe the rumors are true.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.780
I wonder...

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:59.010
If you're scared, you should just head
home, get in bed, and go to sleep.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:02.930
Well, aren't we arrogant...
Maybe you're King?

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:06.430
Well, we'll know the truth soon enough.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.930
This is going to be a lot of fun.

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:12.730
You can have your fun, but don't you think
you're the most likely to go broke next?

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.510
The real pleasure of gambling

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.140
is turning the tables completely
in the final moments of the game.

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:19.620
What are you talking about?!

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.890
You're losing just like
we predicted, aren't you?

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.180
You're totally hopeless without me.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.340
I'll take over from here.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:27.760
Hey, Patty!

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.300
Interesting...

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:33.840
It's best to teach them just how cruel
the world can be while they're still young.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.510
You're...

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:51.160
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:56.400
I heard there was a big poker tournament
on this ship, and I just had to come.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.540
Are you that worried? I'm jealous.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:02.560
It's okay. Your husband hasn't lost anything.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.880
As of yet, at least...

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.470
You're not going to go see him?

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.930
No. It's not like I could
get him to stop anyway.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:10.910
I see.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.810
What? This child is really playing for him?

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:31.150
This isn't a kid's game.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.100
I'm not here for kids' games!

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.350
So you can lose the pompous
attitude until you beat me.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:37.120
Deal the cards!

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.390
What the hell... what's Patty doing here?

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.690
Well now that she's here,
there's nothing we can do about it.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:43.070
Damn...

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:46.220
Well? Did you figure out who this "King" is?

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.660
Not yet. He's a clever one.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:51.480
I guess you just have to keep
winning and stay in it until the end.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.840
Guess so...

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:54.620
It's a risky bet.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.210
But then that's what gambling's
all about, now isn't it?

00:11:58.820 --> 00:11:59.890
Be careful.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:00.840
Sure.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:06.180
Come on, honey, make up your mind.
Are you in or are you out?

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.730
You seem to have aptitude,
but you've got a long way to go.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:12.710
Time for a substitution.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.180
Why! What the heck?!
I was just getting warmed up!

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:16.560
This is my job.

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:18.150
Man...

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:19.020
Nice work.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:23.350
I played it safe like you told
me, but these people are good.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:25.470
Dante's going to get eaten alive...

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.940
That I don't doubt at all.

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:33.010
But Dante's got a job to do, and
that's a game he never loses at.

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:37.760
The only thing we can do now is
have a coffee and pray he succeeds.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:41.350
Fine then. But I'll take tea.
Coffee's too bitter for me.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:41.960
Okay, okay.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:43.340
I fold.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:48.890
Hmmm... Two pairs, eh?

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:53.740
She's the only one who seems
to have a decent hand this time.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:57.370
With those cards,
she could have three of a kind...

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:01.030
If she does, I'm finished.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:06.410
Ah, she always plays with
her hair when she's bluffing...

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:09.610
She's not holding three
of a kind. It's a bluff!

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:13.090
I'll call and raise 8,000.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:15.390
--I fold.
--I fold.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.060
You're smart boys--

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:23.070
I'll call you and raise you 15,000. All in.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:27.440
Trying to bring me down with a bluff?
I see right through you, young lady.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:31.320
Fine, it's on. I'm all in.

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:34.480
I call.

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:38.180
Looks like I got you, Grandpa.

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:39.490
Three of a kind.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:42.150
I win.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.890
So you did get me... Looks
like senility is setting in for me.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:50.890
Please excuse me.

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:54.210
The loser will silently
take his leave from the stage.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.790
Now we know for sure.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:06.260
Someone here is "King."

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:08.720
Let's continue the game.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:12.640
Interesting... But I won't lose
out to anyone with my luck.

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:14.180
You watch, I'll annihilate this "King."

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:19.160
It's just not normal. Don't any of
these people think they can lose?

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.060
Aren't they scared of dying?

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:19.720
Straight flush... I win.

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:20.970
That can't be!

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:24.170
I'm known as Lucky Amanda!

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:27.510
How could I lose...

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:33.680
That's another one. Now it's...

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.480
Yeah. This is the end game.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:37.310
Well, I guess it comes
down to you and me then.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.940
I didn't think you'd be
left standing this long...

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:44.560
If I beat you here, that would make me King!

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.600
Well, deal the cards!

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:54.980
Here we go.

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:07.390
What's with these hands?

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:11.310
So in the end, each of them could
be holding a royal straight flush?!

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:12.760
That's not...

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.180
All in.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.480
You're still on your fourth card.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:20.850
It looks like both of us have
got a final attack to launch.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:24.580
How about we say that whatever
happens next, we showdown?

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:27.200
Fine... So it's all or nothing.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.160
I accept. But I'm low on chips.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:34.220
If I lose, I'll pay the difference
with my life. Sound good?

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.600
Done.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.980
Now, let's have that last card!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:44.160
So, it's a showdown!

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:52.720
A king of hearts! That's
a royal straight flush!

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:53.330
And Dante?!

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:11.510
Royal straight flush.

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:14.260
When two players have the
same hand, spades win.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:17.860
S-Sara... I'm sorry...

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:23.430
He did it! Dante won, Morrison!

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:24.530
Morrison?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.500
There's nothing in this world
as interesting as gambling...

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:33.510
Especially when people
are betting their lives.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:34.090
Dante?!

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:35.980
It's the greatest!

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:42.430
Dante, what are you doing?!

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:46.760
This isn't over yet.
Lady, the next game's against you.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.940
The rules are simple.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.680
Whoever gets a bullet through
the other's heart first, wins.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:52.860
Dante...

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.280
Dante!

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.540
Stop!

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.040
Dante!

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:13.560
Why?! Why would you shoot him,
Lady?! He's your friend, isn't he?!

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:15.970
Let go of me, Morrison! Let go!

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:17.910
Dante!

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.140
Congratulations.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:28.970
I suppose that you are tonight's winner.

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:30.240
You...

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:32.620
So in the end, you're shot
and killed by your own friend.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.440
Not bad... It makes for
quite a beautiful ending.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:36.720
Stay back!

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:40.090
So you're the devil... this King?!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:43.400
You're half right and half wrong.

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:44.330
What do you mean by that?

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:48.960
It didn't matter who played the role of King.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:52.360
Whoever held an item into which
I bestowed my magical powers

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.980
would be captivated by gambling
in exchange for extraordinary luck.

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.810
And that person would act as King.

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:03.330
I wish this man had won for me,
but maybe I was hoping for too much.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.150
So it was a trap from the beginning?

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.110
Please don't fret!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.610
Soon, you'll be as dead as he is.

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:17.790
As will those two, and all
the passengers on the ship!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.090
Sorry to spoil your party...

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:27.910
But I've been waiting for this moment.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:32.130
The moment when you showed
your face to brag about your victory.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.340
Dante!

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:34.640
How did you...

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:37.690
You're wondering if your magic failed on me?

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.800
No, it worked just fine.

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:44.610
I figured out what was
going on by chance, really...

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.120
Patty?

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:57.480
A game, Dante.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:01.450
Let's play a game...
Are you going to die, or am I?

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:02.440
Patty?!

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:03.130
Stop it!

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.820
And that's how I figured it out.

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:15.170
The "mechanism," so to speak, of King.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:19.000
You were using this to turn regular
people into King and control them.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:21.880
So you just pretended to
be possessed by its magic?

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:24.060
No, I was entirely possessed by it.

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:29.150
I knew it was the only way to keep winning,
stay in the game and ultimately draw you out.

00:20:29.150 --> 00:20:30.510
It was a gamble.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:32.850
I avoided hitting your
heart as promised, didn't I?

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:35.150
Actually, you grazed it a bit.
Practice your shooting.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:35.870
Damn...

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:37.320
I've got a lesson for you.

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:40.750
Gambling is something you
do without intermediaries!

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.720
My, my, you're a tough one.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:56.750
You're not going to be able to
harm me with weapons like that.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:59.950
Okay then... How about this?

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:04.800
Dante!

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:24.840
King of hearts.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.100
Ace of spades.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:31.300
I win.

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:45.390
So basically, it was all part of your plan.

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:47.720
You letting yourself be possessed,

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:50.680
then having Lady snap you
out of it if push came to shove?

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:53.260
Hey, I said I was sorry already, didn't I?

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:56.850
Don't sweat the small stuff.
Come on, let's do this.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:22:00.080
You sure sound confident.
You got some good cards?

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:03.140
Hmmm... I'll pass this time.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.720
I'll take three.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:07.530
All right... let's see who's got what.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.590
A full house! How do you like that?

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:15.180
Royal straight flush.

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:17.010
I win.

00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:19.420
We'll just tack your losses onto your debt.

00:22:24.010 --> 00:22:24.820
Damn...

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:27.630
The hell with this.

00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:05.740
My father betrayed demonkind,
and fought for mankind.

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:09.070
from the human perspective,
he's a legendary hero.

00:24:09.070 --> 00:24:12.290
In the minds of the devils, he's
the culprit of an inexcusable crime.

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:15.450
But... There may have been
some devils out there

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:19.370
who could understand my father's thinking.

00:24:20.260 --> 00:24:23.100
If there really is such a devil out there,

00:24:23.890 --> 00:24:27.190
I'd sure like to meet him.